  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 329 PM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nWhile weakening slightly, upper ridging will remain across central \nCONUS. Highs will remain in the low to mid 90s (about 5 to 7 degrees \nabove normal) heading into the late part of next week. While still \nbeing fairly hot, with aid from the cold front that should arrive \nearlier in the week, this should keep our region below further heat \ncriteria. Fire concerns should be kept on the marginal end with \nhumidity values only dropping to the mid 30s and wind gusts largely \nremaining below 25 mph. Near daily isolated thunderstorm chances \nwill continue through Thursday where a couple disturbances are \nforecasted to move through the Northern Plains.",
